## Changed

- Serialized sampling trigger claims with the sample stale-check/publication boundary, preventing a trigger from arriving between generation validation and commit.
- Versioned poll-deadline ownership by state revision, so a delayed older accept cannot reinstall a deadline after a newer authoritative update.
- Replaced separate closed/pending refs with one atomic lifecycle registry: callers are registered before queue offer, and scope closure settles every registered caller exactly once.
- Changed the bounded provider callback bridge to sliding coalescence, preserving the newest authoritative callback (including a terminal event from a disposed attempt) under saturation.

Files touched: `packages/music-core/session/coordinator.ts`, `packages/music-core/session/provider.ts`.

